6-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Four aligned barrows on the South Downs, 3 to 4 metres high despite damage from early digs of which no records survive: the Devil''s Humps, believed Late Neolithic or Early Bronze Age."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-001 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Devil''s Humps are four barrows [S2]; the barrows are aligned [S2]; they are on the South Downs [S1]; they stand 3 to 4 metres high [S2]; they were damaged by early explorations [S2]; no records of those early excavations survive [S3]; they are believed to date from the Late Neolithic or Early Bronze Age [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-002 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Devil''s Humps are barrows (burial mounds) on the South Downs near Stoughton [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil%27s_Humps]; There are four barrows [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil%27s_Humps]; The four barrows are aligned [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil%27s_Humps]; The barrows are 3 to 4 metres high [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil%27s_Humps]; The barrows have been damaged by early digs (explorations) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil%27s_Humps]; No records survive from the early digs [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil%27s_Humps]; Because of that the date of construction is uncertain: the barrows are believed to be Late Neolithic or Early Bronze Age [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil%27s_Humps]; The barrows are Bronze Age monuments, scheduled on the Sussex Downs (Historic England: Bell barrows date to the Early and Middle Bronze Age) [SUPPORTED, no proving quote: https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1008371]"}]'::jsonb),
