 attributed to a queen, Khentkaus II [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid_of_Khentkaus_II]; The queen may have ruled Egypt [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid_of_Khentkaus_II]; The pyramid is now a ruin [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid_of_Khentkaus_II]; The ruin is just 4 metres high [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid_of_Khentkaus_II]; The pyramid was topped by a grey-black granite pyramidion [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid_of_Khentkaus_II]; Fragments of the pyramidion were found in the ruins of the pyramid [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid_of_Khentkaus_II]"}]'::jsonb),
