c595cb24ee4ff21224e3c2acb2529f5"}}'' restored on Bokerley Dyke', '4e4586b4717c4526fc96b692920df8f4ec595cb24ee4ff21224e3c2acb2529f5', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Bokerley Dyke runs 5.75 kilometres across Cranborne Chase. Cut by a Roman road in the 1st century, it was remodelled in the 4th century and the road blocked, shortly after 364 AD."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Bokerley Dyke is 5.75 kilometres long [S1]; it lies on Cranborne Chase [S1]; it was cut by a Roman road in the 1st century [S5]; it was remodelled in the 4th century [S6]; the Roman road was blocked [S6]; this remodelling and blocking dates to shortly after 364 AD [S7]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-008 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Bokerley Dyke is a linear earthwork (a dyke), not a fort or settlement. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bokerley_Dyke]; It runs 5.75 kilometres. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bokerley_Dyke]; It lies on Cranborne Chase (Dorset, England). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bokerley_Dyke]; It was cut through by a Roman road in the 1st century. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bokerley_Dyke]; In the 4th century it was remodelled. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bokerley_Dyke]; Excavations show that the Roman road was blocked. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bokerley_Dyke]; The remodelling and road blocking is dated to shortly after 364 AD. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bokerley_Dyke]"}]'::jsonb),
