; At Pallene it was dedicated to Athena Pallenis. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Ares]; It was moved to the Agora under Augustus. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Ares]; Around 230 fragments of the temple were found. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Ares]; The fragments were found reused in later structures across the Agora. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Ares]; The fragments are of marble. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Ares]"}]'::jsonb),
