ugga]; It is 21 m high [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libyco-Punic_Mausoleum_of_Dougga]; It rises over a five-step pedestal [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libyco-Punic_Mausoleum_of_Dougga]; The lowest level (podium) has false openings [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libyco-Punic_Mausoleum_of_Dougga]; The second level has Ionic columns [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libyco-Punic_Mausoleum_of_Dougga]; The top of the mausoleum is a pyramid [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libyco-Punic_Mausoleum_of_Dougga]; It is royal architecture of Numidia [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libyco-Punic_Mausoleum_of_Dougga]; It dates to the second century BC [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libyco-Punic_Mausoleum_of_Dougga]"}]'::jsonb),
